From 9dae796f6d820050f5dab9b7569edd218bbbc98c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:47:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/30] Add laya.dll: flat C ABI shared library, Delphi binding
 and tests

- capi/: laya_c.h / laya_c.cpp, a JSON-in/JSON-out C ABI over laya::agent
  (create/predict/prepare/info/destroy, error reporting, log callback),
  exception-safe, thread-safe per agent, and FP-environment safe for hosts
  such as Delphi that unmask floating-point exceptions (x87 + MXCSR).
- CMake option LAYA_C_API builds laya.dll / liblaya.so (ggml linked in).
- runtime: laya::set_cpu_threads(); laya-cli --threads N.
- MinGW-w64 cross toolchain + compat header; ws2_32 for laya-http on MinGW.
- tests/capi: C11 test suite, laya-cli parity test, synthetic checkpoint
  generator for testing without downloading weights.
- delphi/: Laya.pas binding, LayaTests.dpr, README.
- .github/workflows/capi-windows.yml: MSVC CPU/Vulkan/CUDA builds + tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
